entals point firmly to the GOP. The state's fifteen-point Republican lean sets the starting point, and no public polls or expert ratings exist to move it.\n\nThe main wrinkle is the rise of home-state governor Andy Beshear, whose national profile and strong approval have fueled talk of a Democratic presidential run. A favorite-son nominee could shave a point or two off the Republican margin, and reports of a broader Democratic surge in Republican-leaning states add some uncertainty. Even so, the evidence for a genuine contest is thin, and Kentucky stays in Likely Republican territory with a wide error band.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0468, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1024, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.09, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1001, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1139, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.083, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1075, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0972, "margin": -14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0925, "margin": -14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1205, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1537, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1065, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.153, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1005, "margin": -14.0}]}